Protocol:
Name	Array Design Protocol
Description	294 non-redundant mature miRNA.
<br>Sequences and 668 non-redundant miRNA sequences from the nine plants (Release 9.0, October 2006; http://microrna.sanger.ac.uk/) were used as microarray probes and each probe repeated four times in one chip. And some control sequences were added as probes for LC internal use. author&#8217;s




Name	Plant growth
Description	Tomato seedlings (cv. Hezuo903) were grown in a growth chamber at 21-26&deg;C, with a 14 h light and 10 h darkness cycle.



Name	labeling protocol
Description	Poly-A tails were added to the small RNAs prepared above at the 3&#8217; ends using a poly(A) polymerase, and Cy3 gain was then ligated to the poly-A tails.

Name	Hybridization protocol
Description	Total RNAs were extracted and small RNAs (< 200 nucleotides) were size-fractionated by utilizing mirVana kit (Ambion, Japan). The tagged RNAs were hybridized to the microfluidic hybridization chip.

Name	Scanning Protocol
Description	Hybridization images were scanned, using a GenePix 4000B microarray scanner (Molecular Devices, Sunnyvale, USA) at 445 nm.

Name	Image analysis protocol
Description	Data extraction and image processing were performed using ArrayPro image analysis software (Media Cybernetics, Silver Spring, USA). The maximum signal level of background probes was set 99.48.

Name	Normalization Protocol
Description	Normalization was performed with a cyclic LOWESS (locally weighted regression) method. A miRNA detection signal threshold was defined as the maximum background signal plus three times of background standard deviation. The maximum signal level of background probes was set 99.48.

